# Shell scripts must stay LF whatever the platform. A CRLF checkout breaks the
# shebang line outright ("bad interpreter: /usr/bin/env bash^M") and, worse here,
# breaks the awk renderers in ways that look like layout bugs rather than line
# endings. Windows clones with core.autocrlf=true would do exactly that.
*.sh        text eol=lf
*.minttyrc  text eol=lf
*.md        text eol=lf
# The Windows side is LF too - that is how the live copies are written, and an
# install that flips endings would back up every file as "changed" for nothing.
*.ps1       text eol=lf
*.vbs       text eol=lf
*.cmd       text eol=lf
*.html      text eol=lf
*.ico       binary
